    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0129" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/12–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Saigon</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Abbott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-30T14:00:00+08:00">December 30,
                            1949—2 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>474. Pass Paris.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d93-f1"/> Pouched Hanoi. In hectic rush
                    ending 2:30 a. m. December 29 agreement reached on about 30 conventions signed
                    today covering transfer powers in following fields: justice, military,
                    economics, finance, public works, cultural affairs, public health, information,
                    personnel.</p>
                <p>Justice convention provides for mixed tribunals for criminal and civil cases
                    involving citizens of French Union and privileged foreigners (Chinese).
                    Presidents mixed courts and state attorneys to be appointed mutual agreement
                    French Vietnam.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Sûreté</hi> entirely transferred Vietnam in principle
                    but French <hi rendition="#italic">Sûreté</hi> will continue control immigration
                    and interstate travel until completion <pb facs="0130" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/>
                    of forthcoming interstate conference, and validate Viet Government passports and
                    travel authorizations until Vietnam achieves international recognition.
                    Counter-espionage and anti-terrorist activities of French <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sûreté</hi> on behalf French Union troops to continue
                    until restoration of order. Only permanent <hi rendition="#italic">Sûreté</hi>
                    organization will be liaison mission with Vietnam <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sûreté</hi> to coordinate security French Union. Viets may have similar
                    mission in Paris.</p>
                <p>Permanent military convention covers bases for and activities of French Union
                    troops. Described by Nguyen Phan Long as more liberal than US–Philippine
                    agreement. Separate agreement covers situation until peace and order
                    restored.</p>
                <p>Above based on summary and analysis furnished Consulate General by French and
                    press interview Nguyen Phan Long. No information re date publication actual
                    texts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abbott</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
